spans.s:
cl. 1. P. न॑मति (Dhātup. xxiii, 12), ˚ते
(mostly intrans.;
cf. Pāṇ. iii, 1, 89;
pr. p. Ā. नमान, R.;
pf. P. नानाम or ननाम, RV. &c.;
2. sg. नेमिथ, or ननन्थ, Vop.;
Subj. नन॑मस्, RV.;
3. pl. नेमुर्, Kāv.;
Ā. नेमे, RV.;
3. pl. -ननामिरे, MBh.;
aor. P. अनान्, Kāṭh.;
अनंसीत्, Daś.;
Ā. अनंस्त Gr.;
3. pl. अनंसत, Br.;
Subj. नंसै, नंसन्ते, RV.;
fut. नंस्यति, Br.;
नमिष्यति, Hariv.;
नन्ता, Siddh.;
inf. -न॑मम्, -न॑मे, RV.;
नन्तुम्, नमितुम्, Kāv.;
ind.p. नत्वा, BhP.; Kathās.;
-नत्य, Br.;
-नम्य, MBh.)
to bend or bow (either trans. or oftener intr.), to bow to, subject or submit one's self (with gen. dat. or acc.), RV. &c. &c.;
 (with हिरुक्) to turn away, keep aside, AV. iv, 1, 3;
to turn towards i.e. to aim at (gen.) with (instr.), RV. i, 165, 6;
to yield or give way, keep quiet or be silent, Bālar. vi, 12;
 (in gram.) to change a dental letter into a cerebral, RPrāt. :
Pass. नम्यते, to be bent or bowed;
 yield or submit to, TUp. iii, 10, 4 :
Caus. नम॑यति, RV. &c. &c. (नामयति, Up. &c.; नाम्यति [!] Mṛcch. i, 30; aor. अनीनमत्, RV.; Pass. नाम्यते, ˚ति, MBh. &c.)
to cause to bow or sink, incline, RV. &c. &c.;
 (with चापम्) to bend a bow, MBh.; Hariv. &c.;
to turn away or ward off, RV.;
to aim at (gen.), ix, 97, 15;
 (in gram.) to change a dental letter into a cerebral, RPrāt. :
Desid. निनंसति, Gr. :
Intens. न॑न्नमीति, RV.;
 नन्नम्यते, KātyŚr. (3. sg. न॑म्नते impf. अनम्नत, p. न॑ममान, RV.) to bow or submit one's self to (dat.), RV.; Br.
